{"text": "Other important and basic patterns that occur in Mathematics are patterns of shapes. These shapes may be in one, two, or three dimensions (1D, 2D, or 3D) — or in even more dimensions. The branch of Mathematics that studies patterns in shapes is called geometry. Shape sequences are one important type of shape pattern that mathematicians study. Table 3 shows a few key shape sequences that are studied in Mathematics.", "pdf_page": 9, "index_on_page": 2, "method": "graph", "cut_concepts": ["MATH6_C0002", "MATH6_C0004"], "chunk_id": "en-ch01-graph-p009-02", "language": "en", "chapter": 1, "chapter_title": "Patterns in Mathematics", "section": "1.5 Patterns in Shapes", "printed_page": 9, "char_start": 464, "char_end": 881, "char_count": 417, "token_count": 109, "truncated_for_embedding": false, "concepts": ["MATH6_C0004", "MATH6_C0002"], "concept_names": ["shape sequences", "pattern"], "primary_concept": "MATH6_C0004", "source_pdf": "fegp101.pdf", "source_clean_file": "assets/extracted/en/en_fegp101_clean.txt", "source_sha256": "704f65089ed97c3bb292a1b708021e321ecf6f68bb61e221b8b9420690b9e063", "citation_url": "/api/textbooks/en/fegp101.pdf#page=9", "method_params": {"max_chars": 450, "min_chars": 200}, "kg_version": "kg-v2-ch1-5", "metadata_version": "chunk-meta-v1"}
