{"text": "1.6 Relation to Number Sequences Often, shape sequences are related to number sequences in surprising ways. Such relationships can be helpful in studying and understanding both the shape sequence and the related number sequence. Example: The number of sides in the shape sequence of Regular Polygons is given by the counting numbers starting at 3, i.e., 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, ....", "pdf_page": 11, "index_on_page": 1, "method": "graph", "cut_concepts": ["MATH6_C0004", "MATH6_C0005", "MATH6_C0014"], "chunk_id": "en-ch01-graph-p011-01", "language": "en", "chapter": 1, "chapter_title": "Patterns in Mathematics", "section": "1.6 Relation to Number Sequences", "printed_page": 11, "char_start": 309, "char_end": 692, "char_count": 383, "token_count": 105, "truncated_for_embedding": false, "concepts": ["MATH6_C0013", "MATH6_C0005", "MATH6_C0014", "MATH6_C0004"], "concept_names": ["counting numbers", "number sequence", "regular polygons", "shape sequences"], "primary_concept": "MATH6_C0013", "source_pdf": "fegp101.pdf", "source_clean_file": "assets/extracted/en/en_fegp101_clean.txt", "source_sha256": "704f65089ed97c3bb292a1b708021e321ecf6f68bb61e221b8b9420690b9e063", "citation_url": "/api/textbooks/en/fegp101.pdf#page=11", "method_params": {"max_chars": 450, "min_chars": 200}, "kg_version": "kg-v2-ch1-5", "metadata_version": "chunk-meta-v1"}
{"text": "That is why these shapes are called, respectively, regular triangle, quadrilateral (i.e., square), pentagon, hexagon, heptagon, octagon, nonagon, decagon, etc., respectively. The word ‘regular’ refers to the fact that these shapes have equal-length sides and also equal ‘angles’ (i.e., the sides look the same and the corners also look the same). We will discuss angles in more depth in the next chapter.", "pdf_page": 11, "index_on_page": 2, "method": "graph", "cut_concepts": [], "chunk_id": "en-ch01-graph-p011-02", "language": "en", "chapter": 1, "chapter_title": "Patterns in Mathematics", "section": "1.6 Relation to Number Sequences", "printed_page": 11, "char_start": 693, "char_end": 1097, "char_count": 404, "token_count": 122, "truncated_for_embedding": false, "concepts": [], "concept_names": [], "primary_concept": null, "source_pdf": "fegp101.pdf", "source_clean_file": "assets/extracted/en/en_fegp101_clean.txt", "source_sha256": "704f65089ed97c3bb292a1b708021e321ecf6f68bb61e221b8b9420690b9e063", "citation_url": "/api/textbooks/en/fegp101.pdf#page=11", "method_params": {"max_chars": 450, "min_chars": 200}, "kg_version": "kg-v2-ch1-5", "metadata_version": "chunk-meta-v1"}
